gs and relevant Cognito User Pool actions (e.g., `cognito-idp:AdminInitiateAuth`, `cognito-idp:SignUp`).\\\\n\\\\nFor each of the 4 roles, please provide the `create-role`, `create-policy` (with the specific inline JSON policy), and `attach-role-policy` commands. Name policies clearly, e.g., `ContactFormLambdaPolicy`.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"4\\\",\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"delta-kaelen-iam-01\\\"\\n}\\n###delta-kaelen-iam-01###\\n###delta-vanto-db-01###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Welcome, Director Vanto. Your task is to define the DynamoDB table schemas for our HOA website project. Your output must be the exact `aws dynamodb create-table` commands for our Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP). \\\\n\\\\nBased on the project architecture, please create commands for the following tables, using `PAY_PER_REQUEST` billing mode:\\\\n1.  **ContactSubmissions**: For logging contact form entries. Use `submissionId` (String) as the partition key.\\\\n2.  **NewsEvents**: For news and blog-style content. Use `postId` (String) as the partition key. Include a Global Secondary Index (GSI) named `status-timestamp-index` with `status` (String) as the partition key and `timestamp` (Number) as the sort key to allow querying for published posts in chronological order.\\\\n3.  **Dues**: For resident dues information. Use `residentId` (String) as the partition key.\\\\n4.  **Meetings**: For annual meeting information. Use `meetingId` (String) as the partition key.\\\\n\\\\nYour final report should contain only the complete, ready-to-execute `aws dynamodb create-table` CLI commands.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"3\\\",\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"delta-vanto-db-01\\\"\\n}\\n###delta-vanto-db-01###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-20T00:39:25.565Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": 