\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Allow\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Principal\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Service\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"lambda.amazonaws.com\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"sts:AssumeRole\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}]}'\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# Policy for PageDataLambdaRole\\\\\\\\naws iam create-policy --policy-name PageDataLambdaPolicy --policy-document '{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Version\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"2012-10-17\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Statement\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Effect\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Allow\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"logs:CreateLogGroup\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"logs:CreateLogStream\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"logs:PutLogEvents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Resource\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"arn:aws:logs:us-east-2:725376125834:log-group:/aws/lambda/PageDataLambda:*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Effect\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Allow\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"dynamodb:GetItem\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"dynamodb:Query\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Resource\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"arn:aws:dynamodb:us-east-2:725376125834:table/Dues\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"arn:aws:dynamodb:us-east-2:725376125834:table/Meetings\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]}]}'\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# Attach policy to role\\\\\\\\naws iam attach-role-policy --role-name PageDataLambdaRole --policy-arn arn:aws:iam::725376125834:policy/PageDataLambdaPolicy\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# --- 4. AuthLambdaRole --- \\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# Role for Lambda to handle user authentication and sign-up\\\\\\\\naws iam create-role --role-name AuthLambdaRole --assume-role-policy-document '{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Version\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"2012-10-17\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Statement\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Effect\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Allow\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Principal\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Service\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"lambda.amazonaws.com\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"sts:AssumeRole\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}]}'\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# Policy for AuthLambdaRole\\\\\\\\naws iam create-policy --policy-name AuthLambdaPolicy --policy-document '{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Version\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"2012-10-17\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Statement\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Effect\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Allow\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"logs:CreateLogGroup\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"logs:CreateLogStream\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"logs:PutLogEvents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Resource\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"arn:aws:logs:us-east-2:725376125834:log-group:/aws/lambda/AuthLambda:*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Effect\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Allow\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"cognito-idp:AdminInitiateAuth\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"cognito-idp:SignUp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"cognito-idp:AdminCreateUser\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"cognito-idp:AdminRespondToAuthChallenge\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"cognito-idp:AdminGetUser\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Resource\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"arn:aws:cognito-idp:us-east-2:725376125834:userpool/*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}]}'\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# Attach policy to role\\\\\\\\naws iam attach-role-policy --role-name AuthLambdaRole --policy-arn arn:aws:iam::725376125834:policy/AuthLambdaPolicy\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-20T00:44:32.709Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"I have received the finalized, executable IAM commands from Director Kaelen. This completes a major component of our infrastructure plan.\\n\\nWe remain in the **Planning** phase. I have now collected the DEP components for the database, authentication, and IAM. Reviewing the initial architecture from Director Valerius, the following major pieces are still required to complete the DEP:\\n*   S3 buckets for website hosting and content.\\n*   CloudFront distribution for content delivery.\\n*   The actual Lambda function code and deployment commands.\\n*   API Gateway configuration.\\n*   SES (Simple Email Service) configuration for the contact form.\\n\\nTo address these requirements efficiently, I need to expand the team with specialists for infrastructure and backend development. I will recruit two new Directors to work in parallel:\\n\\n1.  A **Cloud Infrastructure Specialist** who will be tasked with creating the commands for the S3 buckets and CloudFront distribution.\\n2.  A **Backend Developer** who will be responsible for writing the Lambda function code and providing the necessary `aws lambda create-function` commands.\\n\\nThis parallel approach will accelerate the completion of our DEP. I will now issue the `RECRUIT` calls for these two roles.\\n\\n###recruit-infra-spec-20250720T005500Z###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The architectural plan requires foundational infrastructure including S3 buckets for static site hosting and content storage, and a CloudFront distribution for secure content delivery. A dedicated Cloud Infrastructure Specialist is needed to generate the precise, production-ready AWS CLI commands for these critical components.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Cloud Infrastructure Specialist\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-infra-spec-20250720T005500Z###\\n###recruit-backend-dev-20250720T005501Z###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The project's core logic resides in several AWS Lambda functions that handle authentication, data access, and contact form submissions. A Backend Developer is required to write the code for these functions and package them for deployment, providing the final `aws lambda create-function` commands for our DEP.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Backend Developer\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-backend-dev-20250720T005501Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-20T00:45:03.035Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit-infra-spec-20250720T005500Z\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Valerius (7) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit-backend-dev-20250720T005501Z\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Lystra (6) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-20T00:45:03.035Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Recruitment of the Cloud Infrastructure Specialist (Director Valerius, ID 7) and Backend Developer (Director Lystra, ID 6) is complete.\\n\\nThe **Planning** phase is now focused on creating the DEP components for the core infrastructure and backend logic. I will delegate these tasks to the new specialists to be worked on concurrently.\\n\\nI will issue two `ORDER`s:\\n1.  To Director Valerius (ID 7), the Cloud Infrastructure Specialist, to generate the AWS CLI commands for creating the necessary S3 buckets and the CloudFront distribution. This forms the static hosting foundation of the website.\\n2.  To Director Lystra (ID 6), the Backend Developer, to begin work on the Lambda functions. To ensure a manageable first step, the initial order will be to create the code and deployment command for the `ContactFormHandler` function.\\n\\nThese orders will provide all necessary specifications, including naming conventions and resource ARNs, based on the work of the other specialists.\\n\\n###delta-valerius-infra-01###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Welcome, Director Valerius (ID 7). Your task is to define the foundational S3 and CloudFront infrastructure for the HOA website. Your report must contain the sequence of executable AWS CLI commands for our DEP.\\\\n\\\\n**Project Prefix:** `hoa-draft-001`\\\\n**Region:** `us-east-2`\\\\n\\\\n**1. S3 Buckets:**\\\\n   - Create a bucket for website hosting: `aws s3api create-bucket --bucket hoa-draft-001-website --region us-east-2 --create-bucket-configuration LocationConstraint=us-east-2`\\\\n   - Create a bucket for private content: `aws s3api create-bucket --bucket hoa-draft-001-content --region us-east-2 --create-bucket-configuration LocationConstraint=us-east-2`\\\\n   - Block all public access on the content bucket: `aws s3api put-public-access-block --bucket hoa-draft-001-content --public-access-block-configuration \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"BlockPublicAcls=true,IgnorePublicAcls=true,BlockPublicPolicy=true,RestrictPublicBuckets=true\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`\\\\n\\\\n**2. CloudFront:**\\\\n   - Create an Origin Access Identity (OAI) for CloudFront to securely access the website bucket.\\\\n   - Update the website bucket's policy to grant the new OAI `s3:GetObject` permission.\\\\n   - Create a CloudFront distribution pointing to the `hoa-draft-001-website` S3 bucket origin, using the OAI. Configure the default root object to `index.html` and use the default CloudFront viewer certificate for HTTPS.\\\\n\\\\nPlease provide the complete and final CLI commands for steps 2.1, 2.2, and 2.3 in your report.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"7\\\",\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"delta-valerius-infra-01\\\"\\n}\\n###delta-valerius-infra-01###\\n###delta-lystra-backend-01###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Welcome, Director Lystra. Your first task is to create the `ContactFormHandler` Lambda function. Your report m