\\\\n\\\\\\\\n        name = body.get('name')\\\\\\\\n        email = body.get('email')\\\\\\\\n        message = body.get('message')\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n        if not (name and email and message):\\\\\\\\n            return {\\\\\\\\n                'statusCode': 400,\\\\\\\\n                'body': json.dumps({'error': 'Missing required fields.'})\\\\\\\\n            }\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n        submission_id = str(uuid.uuid4())\\\\\\\\n        timestamp = datetime.utcnow().isoformat()\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n        table = dynamodb.Table(TABLE_NAME)\\\\\\\\n        table.put_item(Item={\\\\\\\\n            'SubmissionId': submission_id,\\\\\\\\n            'Name': name,\\\\\\\\n            'Email': email,\\\\\\\\n            'Message': message,\\\\\\\\n            'Timestamp': timestamp\\\\\\\\n        })\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n        ses.send_email(\\\\\\\\n            Source=SOURCE_EMAIL,\\\\\\\\n            Destination={'ToAddresses': [DEST_EMAIL]},\\\\\\\\n            Message={\\\\\\\\n                'Subject': {'Data': 'New Contact Form Submission'},\\\\\\\\n                'Body': {\\\\\\\\n                    'Text': {\\\\\\\\n                        'Data': (\\\\\\\\n                            f'Contact Form Submission\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n'\\\\\\\\n                            f'ID: {submission_id}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n'\\\\\\\\n                            f'Name: {name}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n'\\\\\\\\n                            f'Email: {email}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n'\\\\\\\\n                            f'Message:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n{message}'\\\\\\\\n                        )\\\\\\\\n                    }\\\\\\\\n                }\\\\\\\\n            }\\\\\\\\n        )\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n        return {\\\\\\\\n            'statusCode': 200,\\\\\\\\n            'body': json.dumps({'message': 'Submission received.', 'submissionId': submission_id})\\\\\\\\n        }\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    except Exception as e:\\\\\\\\n        return {\\\\\\\\n            'statusCode': 500,\\\\\\\\n            'body': json.dumps({'error': str(e)})\\\\\\\\n        }\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAWS CLI deployment command:\\\\\\\\naws lambda create-function --function-name ContactFormHandler --runtime python3.9 --role arn:aws:iam::725376125834:role/ContactFormLambdaRole --handler contact_form_handler.lambda_handler --zip-file fileb://contact_form_handler.zip\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-20T00:46:53.472Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"I have received the reports from Director Valerius (Infrastructure) and Director Lystra (Backend).\\n\\nDirector Lystra's report for the `ContactFormHandler` Lambda is complete and provides the necessary Python code and a deployment command. This is a solid component for our plan.\\n\\nHowever, Director Valerius's report for the CloudFront infrastructure has revealed a critical flaw in our current planning methodology. The commands for creating an Origin Access Identity (OAI) and then using its generated ID in subsequent commands are not deterministically executable in a single pass. This multi-step, state-dependent process violates the core requirement of a DEP. It would require manual intervention or a more complex, stateful execution engine, which we do not have.\\n\\nThis insight necessitates a strategic pivot in our planning approach. The most robust and appropriate solution to manage interdependent cloud resources is to use an infrastructure-as-code (IaC) service. For AWS, this is **AWS CloudFormation**. A single CloudFormation template can define all our resources—IAM roles, DynamoDB tables, S3 buckets, Cognito pools, Lambda functions (with inline code), and CloudFront distributions—and CloudFormation itself will resolve the dependencies during deployment.\\n\\nThis is a superior strategy that ensures a truly deterministic, single-step execution of our entire plan.\\n\\nTherefore, our new **Planning** objective is to create a single, comprehensive CloudFormation template. To achieve this, I will recruit a specialist with the necessary expertise.\\n\\nMy next action is to recruit a \\\"CloudFormation Architect\\\". This agent will be tasked with consolidating all previously gathered components into a master template and defining the remaining pieces of our architecture.\\n\\n###recruit-cfn-arch-20250720T005800Z###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The project's complexity requires a more robust deployment method than sequential CLI commands. An AWS CloudFormation Architect is needed to consolidate all defined resources (IAM, DynamoDB, Cognito, S3, Lambda) into a single, comprehensive template. This ensures a deterministic, atomic, and repeatable deployment, which is critical for the success and maintainability of the project.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"CloudFormation Architect\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-cfn-arch-20250720T005800Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-20T00:47:52.570Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit-cfn-arch-20250720T005800Z\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Grymm (8) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-20T00:47:52.570Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Recruitment of the CloudFormation Architect, Director Grymm, is complete. The firm's strategy has successfully pivoted to using AWS CloudFormation, which will produce a more robust and truly deterministic plan.\\n\\nThe **Planning** phase continues with the new objective of creating a single, comprehensive CloudFormation template. Before I can task 