38@gmail.com\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-20T00:48:49.327Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"I have received the user's administrative email address, `ethanm938@gmail.com`. This is the final piece of information required for our new strategic approach.\\n\\nThe **Planning** phase has now fully pivoted to creating a single, comprehensive AWS CloudFormation template. This will encapsulate the entire project infrastructure, ensuring a deterministic and atomic deployment. Director Grymm (ID: 8), our CloudFormation Architect, will be responsible for this critical task.\\n\\nI will now issue a detailed and comprehensive `ORDER` to Director Grymm. This order will serve as the master specification, consolidating all the requirements, resource definitions, and code gathered from the entire team's efforts into a single directive. The successful completion of this order will yield our final Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP).\\n\\n###delta-grymm-cfn-01###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Welcome, Director Grymm. Your sole task is to create a single, complete AWS CloudFormation template in YAML format. This template will define the entire infrastructure for the HOA website project and will be our final DEP. Consolidate all requirements from previous specialists into this one file.\\\\n\\\\n**Parameters:**\\\\n- `ProjectPrefix`: Default value `hoa-draft-001`.\\\\n- `AdminEmail`: Default value `ethanm938@gmail.com`.\\\\n\\\\n**Resources to Define:**\\\\n1.  **S3 & CloudFront:**\\\\n    - `WebsiteBucket`: S3 bucket for static hosting.\\\\n    - `ContentBucket`: S3 bucket for private content (e.g., images for news posts), with public access blocked.\\\\n    - `CloudFrontOAI`: An Origin Access Identity.\\\\n    - `WebsiteBucketPolicy`: Grants the OAI `s3:GetObject` access to the `WebsiteBucket`.\\\\n    - `CloudFrontDistribution`: Serves the `WebsiteBucket` via the OAI, redirects HTTP to HTTPS, and sets `index.html` as the default root object.\\\\n\\\\n2.  **DynamoDB Tables (BillingMode: PAY_PER_REQUEST):**\\\\n    - `ContactSubmissionsTable`: PK: `submissionId` (String).\\\\n    - `NewsEventsTable`: PK: `postId` (String). GSI: `status-timestamp-index` (PK: `status` (String), SK: `timestamp` (Number)).\\\\n    - `DuesTable`: PK: `residentId` (String).\\\\n    - `MeetingsTable`: PK: `meetingId` (String).\\\\n\\\\n3.  **Cognito:**\\\\n    - `UserPool`: Name based on `ProjectPrefix`, email as username alias, standard attributes `name` and `email` required, strict password policy, admin-create-user-only configuration.\\\\n    - `UserPoolClient`: A web client for the user pool.\\\\n\\\\n4.  **IAM Roles & Policies (Use intrinsic functions like `!GetAtt` and `!Ref` to link resources):**\\\\n    - `ContactFormLambdaRole`: Permissions for CloudWatch Logs, `dynamodb:PutItem` on `ContactSubmissionsTable`, and `ses:SendEmail`.\\\\n\\\\n5.  **SES:**\\\\n    - `SESIdentity`: An `AWS::SES::EmailIdentity` resource to verify the `AdminEmail` parameter.\\\\n\\\\n6.  **Lambda Function (Runtime: python3.9):**\\\\n    - `ContactFormHandler`: Use the IAM role above. Pass the `ContactSubmissionsTable` name and `AdminEmail` as environment variables. The function code is provided below. You must inline this code within the CloudFormation template under the `Code` property.\\\\n\\\\n7.  **API Gateway:**\\\\n    - `RestApi`: A REST API resource.\\\\n    - `/contact` path with a `POST` method.\\\\n    - A Lambda integration connecting the `POST` method to the `ContactFormHandler` function.\\\\n    - Enable CORS on the resource.\\\\n\\\\n8.  **Outputs:**\\\\n    - `WebsiteURL`: The domain name of the `CloudFrontDistribution`.\\\\n    - `UserPoolId`: The ID of the `UserPool`.\\\\n    - `UserPoolClientId`: The ID of the `UserPoolClient`.\\\\n    - `ApiGatewayEndpoint`: The invoke URL for the API Gateway stage.\\\\n\\\\n**Lambda Code for `ContactFormHandler` (to be inlined):**\\\\n```python\\\\nimport json\\\\nimport uuid\\\\nimport os\\\\nfrom datetime import datetime\\\\nimport boto3\\\\n\\\\ndynamodb = boto3.resource('dynamodb')\\\\nses = boto3.client('ses')\\\\n\\\\nTABLE_NAME = os.environ['CONTACT_TABLE']\\\\nDEST_EMAIL = os.environ['DEST_EMAIL']\\\\nSOURCE_EMAIL = 'no-reply@' + os.environ['DOMAIN_NAME'] # Construct dynamically if possible, else hardcode a placeholder domain.\\\\n\\\\ndef lambda_handler(event, context):\\\\n    try:\\\\n        body = json.loads(event.get('body', '{}'))\\\\n        name = body.get('name')\\\\n        email = body.get('email')\\\\n        message = body.get('message')\\\\n        if not (name and email and message):\\\\n            return {'statusCode': 400, 'body': json.dumps({'error': 'Missing required fields.'})}\\\\n\\\\n        submission_id = str(uuid.uuid4())\\\\n        table = dynamodb.Table(TABLE_NAME)\\\\n        table.put_item(Item={'submissionId': submission_id, 'name': name, 'email': email, 'message': message, 'timestamp': datetime.utcnow().isoformat()})\\\\n\\\\n        ses.send_email(\\\\n            Source=SOURCE_EMAIL,\\\\n            Destination={'ToAddresses': [DEST_EMAIL]},\\\\n            Message={\\\\n                'Subject': {'Data': 'New Contact Form Submission'},\\\\n                'Body': {'Text': {'Data': f'Name: {name}\\\\\\\\nEmail: {email}\\\\\\\\nMessage: {message}'}}\\\\n            }\\\\n        )\\\\n        return {'statusCode': 200, 'body': json.dumps({'message': 'Submission received.'})}\\\\n    except Exception as e:\\\\n        return {'statusCode': 500, 'body': json.dumps({'error': str(e)})}\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nYour final report should contain only the complete, final CloudFormation YAML template.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"8\\\",\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"delta-grymm-cfn-01\\\"\\n}\\n###delta-grymm-cfn-01###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-20T00:51:00.778Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Depa