\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Joric (5) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-20T00:43:17.460Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Recruitment of the Authentication Specialist, Director Joric, is successful.\\n\\nWe remain in the **Planning** phase. The immediate priority is to define the authentication component, which is a prerequisite for completing the IAM policies. I will now delegate this task to the new specialist.\\n\\nI will issue an `ORDER` to Director Joric (ID: 5), instructing them to generate the AWS CLI command for creating the Cognito User Pool. I will provide the project prefix to ensure consistent naming and specify the necessary configurations for the HOA website's authentication model. This will provide the final piece of information (the Cognito User Pool name) needed to complete the IAM policies.\\n\\n###delta-joric-auth-01###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Welcome, Director Joric. Your task is to define the AWS Cognito User Pool for our HOA website project. Your output must be a single, complete, and executable `aws cognito-idp create-user-pool` command for our DEP.\\\\n\\\\n**Requirements for the User Pool:**\\\\n1.  **Pool Name:** Use the project prefix `hoa-draft-001` to name the pool `hoa-draft-001-user-pool`.\\\\n2.  **Sign-in Options:** Configure `email` as a sign-in alias.\\\\n3.  **User Attributes:** Require the `email` and `name` standard attributes.\\\\n4.  **Security:** Set a password policy with a minimum length of 8 characters, requiring numbers, symbols, uppercase, and lowercase letters.\\\\n5.  **User Registration:** Configure the pool so that only administrators can create users (`admin-create-user-config`). This is for the initial setup where an HOA admin would add residents.\\\\n\\\\nYour final report should contain only the complete, ready-to-execute `aws cognito-idp create-user-pool` CLI command.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"5\\\",\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"delta-joric-auth-01\\\"\\n}\\n###delta-joric-auth-01###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-20T00:43:43.396Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"delta-joric-auth-01\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order delta-joric-auth-01 from agent 5: aws cognito-idp create-user-pool --pool-name hoa-draft-001-user-pool --username-attributes email --auto-verified-attributes email --schema Name=email,AttributeDataType=String,Required=true,Mutable=true Name=name,AttributeDataType=String,Required=true,Mutable=true --policies '{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"PasswordPolicy\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"MinimumLength\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":8,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"RequireUppercase\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":true,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"RequireLowercase\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":true,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"RequireNumbers\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":true,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"RequireSymbols\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":true}}' --admin-create-user-config '{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"AllowAdminCreateUserOnly\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":true}' --mfa-configuration OFF\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-20T00:43:43.396Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"I have received the report from Director Joric containing the `aws cognito-idp create-user-pool` command. This command is approved and will be part of the final DEP.\\n\\nWith this, I now have all the information required to construct the final IAM policies. The initial report from the IAM specialist, Director Kaelen, contained placeholders. I will now issue a new order to Director Kaelen to regenerate the IAM commands with the concrete values we have now acquired.\\n\\nA key challenge is that the Cognito User Pool ARN requires a Pool ID, which is only generated upon creation. To create a fully deterministic plan *before* execution, I will instruct Director Kaelen to use a wildcard for the resource part of the Cognito ARN (`arn:aws:cognito-idp:us-east-2:725376125834:userpool/*`). While not ideal from a least-privilege perspective, it is a necessary compromise to enable the creation of a static, single-phase DEP. This is an acceptable trade-off for this project's scope.\\n\\nI will now issue the updated order to Director Kaelen (ID: 4).\\n\\n###delta-kaelen-iam-02###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Director Kaelen, thank you for your initial report. We now have the final values required to complete the IAM commands. Please regenerate your report, replacing all placeholders with the following concrete values. The output must be a sequence of complete and executable AWS CLI commands with no remaining placeholders.\\\\n\\\\n**Values for Substitution:**\\\\n*   `<AWS_ACCOUNT_ID>`: `725376125834`\\\\n*   `<AWS_REGION>`: `us-east-2`\\\\n*   `<CONTENT_BUCKET_NAME>`: `hoa-draft-001-content`\\\\n*   `<COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID>`: For the `AuthLambdaPolicy` resource ARN, please use a wildcard to ensure the command is executable before the pool is created. The ARN should be: `arn:aws:cognito-idp:us-east-2:725376125834:userpool/*`\\\\n\\\\nPlease provide the final, complete `aws iam create-role`, `aws iam create-policy`, and `aws iam attach-role-policy` commands for all four roles as previously specified, with these values correctly substituted.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"4\\\",\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"delta-kaelen-iam-02\\\"\\n}\\n###delta-kaelen-iam-02###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-20T00:44:32.709Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\